\subsection{Results discussion}
As illustrated in previous examples, the accuracy of the results in this study hinges on the precision of predicting $\bm \Theta$. A precise prediction ensures that the ML-ROM aligns with the POD-ROM solution, which, for this case and all snapshots, exhibits negligible discrepancies from the FEM solution.\\

In this example, Random Forest is used for predicting the values of $\bm \Theta$. The Grid Search Cross Validation methodology (GridSearch) \cite{GridSearch} is used to optimize the Random Forest parameters. The chosen configuration includes 50 estimators, 4 minimum sample leaves, 70 random states, and the use of bootstrap. In fact, for complex study cases, Grid Search can act as an automation tool to efficiently select the optimal Random Forest parameters, reducing the reliance on user trial and error.\\

For simplicity, we refrain from showcasing all $\bm \theta_k$ values for $k \in[1,9]$. Instead, we focus primarily on $\bm \theta_1$, which holds the most significant impact on results, and $\bm \theta_9$, which has the least impact and is generally is the most challenging to predict accurately.\\

