In what follows, we regard $V$ as the set of integers $\set{1, \ldots, \size{V}}$ to simplify the discussion.

Let $\mathcal H = (V, \mathcal E)$ be a hypergraph.
To simplify our proof, we assume that $\mathcal H$ has at least two vertices.
Furthermore, we can assume that $\mathcal H$ has no independent sets with cardinality $\size{V}-1$.
