\begin{theorem}[a quasi-Carleman estimate, \cite{MFG2}, section
2.3.2 of \cite{MFGbook}] \label{Theorem 3.2}. {Let the number }$c${\ be the same as in (\ref%
{4.01}), (\ref{4.02}). Let the function }$g\in C^{1}\left( \overline{Q}%
_{T}\right) ${.\ Then there exists a sufficiently large number }$%
\lambda _{0,2}=\lambda _{0,2}\left( c,\left\Vert g\right\Vert _{C^{1}\left( 
\overline{Q}_{T}\right) },Q_{T}\right) \geq 1$ {depending only on
