\subsection{An Interesting Observation}

An interesting phenomenon, which one can observe from (\ref{num:rel-cost})
and Figures \ref{fig:1-cost-extended}, \ref{fig:C21-cost}, \ref{fig:C22-cost}%
, and \ref{fig:C23-cost} is that for small times $t\in \left( 0,0.3\right) $%
, the minimizer of our target functional (\ref{5.6}) does not satisfy well
to the MFG system (\ref{num:1})-(\ref{num:2}) for all considered cases, even
for the ideal initial conditions. On the other hand, it satisfies that
system well for $t\in \left[ 0.3,1\right) $. Finally, the instability for
the function $u(x,t)$ takes over for $t>1$, see Figure \ref%
{fig:1-cost-extended}.

