This makes ZC sequences less suitable for high Doppler scenarios, e.g., LEO-based systems (Doppler shifts typically on the order of 30-40 kHz). %Such scenarios require  Doppler shifts to be accurately estimated and corrected, even if Doppler-based positioning methods are not explicitly employed, as they can introduce significant range errors~\cite{9144242}. 
On the other hand, Bj\"orck sequences not only prove to be superior to Gold sequences in terms of autocorrelation but also exhibit a better ambiguity function than ZC sequences, facilitating accurate time and frequency offset estimation. Even when compared to Gold sequences, Bj\"orck sequences show a clear advantage in their ambiguity function, offering better peak sharpness and reduced sidelobes next to the main peak. With that understanding, we now proceed with a comprehensive study of Bj\"orck sequences in the subsequent sections.
