$\delta(2\alpha^{si})=t^2$ for $2t\mid p^m+1$, $1\leq i< \frac{p^m+1}{t}$ and $\alpha^{si}\neq-1$.
\item[(vii)] if $2t\nmid p^m+1$, then $\delta(\alpha^{si}-\alpha^{sj})
    =t^2$, where $1\leq i,j< \frac{p^m+1}{t}$ and $i\neq j$.
\item[(vii)] if $2t\mid p^m+1$, then $\delta(\alpha^{si}-\alpha^{sj})
