% We propose Ming-Omni, a unified multimodal model that can process a wide range of inputs, including images, text, audio, and video, and deliver both speech and image generation with remarkable proficiency. 
\abstract{\fontsize{11pt}{12pt} \textit{We propose Ming-Omni, a unified multimodal model capable of processing images, text, audio, and video, while demonstrating strong proficiency in both speech and image generation.
% 
% By utilizing dedicated encoders, Ming-Omni extracts tokens from different modalities and processes them through Ling, an MoE architecture which is equipped with newly proposed modality-specific routers. 
Ming-Omni employs dedicated encoders to extract tokens from different modalities, which are then processed by Ling, an MoE architecture equipped with newly proposed modality-specific routers.
% 
% This design allows for efficient handling of multimodal data and ensures that the model can effectively integrate information from various modalities. 
This design enables a single model to efficiently process and fuse multimodal inputs within \textbf{a unified framework}, thereby facilitating diverse tasks without requiring separate models, task-specific fine-tuning, or structural redesign.
% 
% Ming-Omni is equipped with an advanced audio decoder that produces natural-sounding speech, as well as MetaQueries, which enables high-quality image generation. 
% 
% These features allow the model to engage in context-aware chatting, perform text-to-speech conversion, and conduct versatile image editing. 
% 
Importantly, Ming-Omni extends beyond conventional multimodal models by supporting audio and image generation. This is achieved through the integration of an advanced audio decoder for natural-sounding speech and Ming-Lite-Uni for high-quality image generation, which also allow the model to engage in context-aware chatting, perform text-to-speech conversion, and conduct versatile image editing. 
% 
% Our experimental results demonstrate that Ming-Omni offers a powerful solution for unified perception and generation across all modalities.
% 
% By leveraging a fixed MLLM and a learnable diffusion model, \model{} enhances the image generation and editing capabilities of multimodal understanding models.
%
% Unlike previous approaches that rely on separate diffusion models or other decoders, \model{} allows the autoregressive model to learn contextual dependencies across consistent multimodal tokens, making the two tasks mutually beneficial and adaptable.
%
% Within the \textbf{Multi-Scale Learnable Query Tokens} and \textbf{Connector}, a single autoregressive model learns cross-modal context, allowing visual comprehension and image synthesis objectives to reinforce one another. 
% 
% 
%
% This unified design supports natural, dialog-based interactions for tasks such as pixel-level image editing and multimodal understanding. 
% 
Our experimental results showcase Ming-Omni offers a powerful solution for unified perception and generation across all modalities.
%
%% The core idea behind the choice technical approach followed by \model{} is to enable native multimodal training of a autoregressive model, where understanding, image generation, and potentially additional visual modalities such as video can all be represented and learned within a \textbf{shared high-dimensional feature space} (\textit{e.g.}, $1024$ dimensions).
% \model{} shows impressive capabilities in dialog-driven image generation and editing, achieving highly intelligence with the fluid nature of its interactive process.
%
% To the best of our knowledge, Ming-Omni is the first open-source model to achieve parity with GPT4o's capabilities in modality support. We release all code and model weights to foster further exploration within the community. 
% 
Notably, our proposed Ming-Omni is the first open-source model we are aware of to match GPT-4o in modality support, and we release all code and model weights to encourage further research and development in the community.
