\section{Results}
\subsection{Strengths, Weaknesses, and Unmet User Needs for Surgical Training Environment (RQ1)}
Our surgical trainees had experience with various training environments, including open surgery training, robotic console training simulations, and dual robotic consoles for training under experts' supervision. The robotic console provides a VR simulator for robotic surgery, while the dual console allows trainees to observe experts during robotic surgery on patients. The robotic consoles provided training exclusively for robotic surgeries so they cannot be used for training endoscopic skills, but we list them because they provided the trainees VR and AR training exposure and informed their co-designs. However, their exposure to these systems varied based on their post-graduation years \autoref{tab:demographics}. 
