For ordinary de Bruijn graphs over a binary alphabet, the general structure of the sandpile group has been %discovered 
described by Levine~\cite{DBLP:journals/jct/Levine11}:
 \begin{equation}\label{Levine}
     K(\DB(2,2^d))\cong \bigoplus_{i=1}^{d-1}(\Z_{2^i})^{2^{d-1-i}}.
 \end{equation}

In the case of generalized de Bruijn graphs, Chan, Hollmann and Pasechnik gave the structure of $K(\DB(k, n))$ for arbitrary $k$ and $n$~\cite[Theorem 3.1]{ECCGTA13}. We refer the reader to~\cite{ECCGTA13,CHAN2015268} for further details.

